<h2 id="v1-7-2">Version 1.7.2</h2>

<p><strong>Released:</strong> November 17, 2026<br>
<strong>Focus:</strong> Corrections found while planning a site with no domain or license yet</p>

<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The nav partial (4.14) now opens its mobile menu. It put a <code>toggle</code> controller on the button and the menu's <code>toggle</code> target outside the button, so Stimulus never found the target. The partial now uses <code>mobile-nav</code> (4.6), wired as that controller's own usage comment shows</li>
</ul>

<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The head partial (4.13) writes the canonical link, <code>og:url</code>, and <code>og:image</code> only when <code>site.url</code> is known. A site built before its domain is chosen leaves <code>url</code> out, or marks it <code>blank()</code>, and guesses no address</li>
  <li>The footer partial (4.15) takes its rights statement from <code>site.rights</code>, with "All rights reserved." when it is left out</li>
  <li>Section 3 lists two optional folders that sites built to the spec already use: <code>scripts/</code> and <code>docs/</code></li>
  <li>Section 3 lists optional root license files, <code>LICENSE</code> and <code>LICENSE-CONTENT.md</code>, for a site that licenses its content apart from its code</li>
  <li>Any site may add the <code>test</code> script. It was for scene sites only</li>
  <li>The deploy workflow runs the tests before the build, and skips them when a site has none</li>
  <li>Node 22 replaces Node 20, which reached end of life on 30 April 2026</li>
  <li>Section 3 lists optional extra workflows in <code>.github/workflows/</code> and an optional <code>.claude/</code> folder for agent hooks and settings</li>
  <li>Section 3 lists an optional <code>kit/</code> folder for kits the site distributes but does not render, such as a coding-agent plugin</li>
  <li>The print styles no longer print "Printed from {{ '{{' }} site.url }}". CSS cannot run a template, so every site printed that text literally</li>
</ul>

<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
  <li>A search gate: <code>site.indexable: false</code> makes the head write <code>&lt;meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"&gt;</code> on every page. The note says why a robots.txt Disallow is optional, citing <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/block-indexing">Google's documentation</a></li>
  <li>Stack Decisions names the one exception to injecting globals: <code>eleventy.config.js</code> may read <code>process.env.NODE_ENV</code> and <code>new Date()</code></li>
  <li>The quality checklist checks that the mobile menu opens and closes at phone width, that the workflow runs the tests, and that the search gate holds on every page</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="v1-7-1">Version 1.7.1</h2>

<p><strong>Released:</strong> October 9, 2026<br>
<strong>Focus:</strong> Corrections to Scene Sites</p>

<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ '/scene-sites/#fallback-and-motion' | url }}">Fallback and Motion</a> names two forms of fallback: a hidden fallback element, or the plain page with the scene opting in through a <code>has-scene</code> class (first used in vetmgmedia.com's sort section, in review)</li>
  <li>"Never drawn into the canvas" is now "the canvas may repeat the page's words, never replace them." The old wording was contradicted by this site's own Blueprint homepage, which draws labels on its canvas</li>
  <li>The Scene Checklist checks that every word the canvas draws is also in the HTML</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="v1-7-0">Version 1.7.0</h2>

<p><strong>Released:</strong> October 9, 2026<br>
<strong>Focus:</strong> Scene sites</p>

<p>Learnings from three scene sites (Harmonices Mundi, Center of Percussion, Metes &amp; Bounds) that had converged on the same shape inside this stack without the spec describing it, proved by porting a fourth, <a href="https://dannycaruso.link">dannycaruso.link</a>, onto it.</p>

<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ '/scene-sites/' | url }}">Scene Sites</a>: an optional layer for sites with a live rendered scene steered by scrolling</li>
  <li><code>chapter</code> controller: announces its look on <code>&lt;scene&gt;:chapter</code> when it straddles mid-screen, and <code>&lt;scene&gt;:approach</code> as it comes up from below</li>
  <li>The scene controller pattern: one joint owns the frame loop and every browser global</li>
  <li><code>src/assets/js/lib/</code> for scene logic, renderer, and domain math</li>
  <li>Renderer contract: WebGL2 renderers throw when unavailable, and the page shows a static fallback</li>
  <li><code>test</code> script (<code>node --test</code>) and <code>test/</code> directory for scene sites</li>
  <li><a href="{{ '/content/#facts-not-yet-known' | url }}">Facts Not Yet Known</a>: <code>blank()</code> markers and a <code>fact</code> macro</li>
</ul>

<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Directory structure lists <code>lib/</code> and <code>test/</code></li>
  <li>npm scripts list <code>test</code> for scene sites</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="v1-6-0">Version 1.6.0</h2>

<p><strong>Released:</strong> January 9, 2026<br>
<strong>Focus:</strong> Analytics and accessibility patterns</p>

<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>analytics</code> controller for GA4 event tracking (tel/mailto/sms)</li>
  <li><code>forms.json</code> data file for centralized dropdown options</li>
  <li><code>og_title</code> and <code>og_description</code> frontmatter overrides</li>
  <li><code>bodyClass</code> frontmatter for per-page body styling</li>
  <li><code>highlight: true</code> navigation field for CTA styling</li>
  <li>CSS utilities: <code>scale-102</code>, <code>gradient-text</code></li>
  <li>Animation keyframes: <code>fade-in</code>, <code>slide-in-up</code>, <code>slide-in-left</code></li>
  <li><code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> accessibility media query</li>
</ul>

<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
  <li>head.njk cascades og_title → title → site.name for OG meta</li>
  <li>base.njk body tag supports dynamic bodyClass</li>
</ul>

